<hr>
<h2>11. Radiology NLP</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Model</strong>: XLM-R-base (multilingual robustness); if report=
s are verified English-only, ClinicalBERT/PubMedBERT is slightly better for=
 medical text. Do not verify-by-assumption: detect language per report (fas=
tText/lingua) and inspect; keep XLM-R as the safe default.</li>
<li><strong>Prefer structured extraction over free-text fusion.</strong> Bu=
ild a keyword/regex + model-hybrid extractor mapping report sentences =E2=
=86=92 per-structure per-finding indicators (present/absent/uncertain) for =
the 12 targets plus free-text negatives. This directly addresses negation (=
"intact ACL", "no joint effusion") and uncertainty ("? meniscal tear", "can=
not exclude"), which raw XLM-R embeddings handle unreliably in clinical, po=
ssibly non-English prose. The extracted per-label sentiment (=E2=88=921/0/+=
1) becomes (a) teacher supervision enrichment and (b) pseudo-label auxiliar=
y targets. Full report understanding (radNLP SOTA) is unnecessary because t=
he 12 labels already define the output space.</li>
<li>Validate the extractor manually on ~100 reports; measure extraction F1 =
per label before trusting it.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>12. DICOM pipeline</h2>
<p>Libraries: <strong>pydicom</strong> (header/pixels), <strong>SimpleITK o=
r MONAI transforms</strong> (resampling/normalization), OpenCV only for res=
ize.</p>
<p>Pipeline per series:</p>
<ol>
<li>Load all SOPs with pydicom; handle transfer syntaxes (JPEG lossless var=
iants, deflated) via GDCM/Pillow handlers; fallback decode guard.</li>
<li><strong>Sort by ImagePositionPatient projected onto the slice normal</s=
trong> n =3D row=C3=97col from ImageOrientationPatient =E2=80=94 <em>never =
filename order</em> (filenames can be scrambled, and some series have non-i=
nteger or reversed orderings). Handle multi-frame DICOM (check NumberOfFram=
es).</li>
<li>Resample spacing: keep native in-plane spacing; enforce consistent slic=
e step by resampling along z to a fixed effective thickness (e.g., 1.0=E2=
=80=931.5 mm) only for 3D models; for the 2.5D slice model, simply sample 6=
4 evenly spaced sorted slices.</li>
<li>Normalize: per-series percentile-clip (0.5=E2=80=9399.5) =E2=86=92 z-sc=
ore.</li>
<li>Crop: center-crop/auto-crop to the knee bounding box (threshold-based b=
ounding box of nonzero signal) =E2=86=92 resize 320=C2=B2.</li>
<li>Sanity checks per study: orientation consistency across series (cosine =
of normals), duplicate SOPInstanceUIDs, missing pixel data =E2=80=94 log &a=
mp; exclude/repair; never let one corrupt study poison a training run.</li>
</ol>
<p>Cache decoded, sorted volumes as .npy/zarr (uint8 after scaling) keyed b=
y SeriesInstanceUID =E2=80=94 the single biggest throughput win.</p>
<hr>
<h2>13. Validation strategy</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>5-fold GroupKFold by StudyInstanceUID</strong> (equivalently pa=
tient; assume StudyInstanceUID =E2=89=88 patient encounter). Verify no pati=
ent/series overlap across folds; additionally hash-dedupe studies with near=
-identical pixel data (repeated acquisitions) and keep them in the same fol=
d.</li>
<li><strong>Multi-label stratification</strong>: iterative stratification (=
Sechidis et al.; <code>iterative-stratification</code> package) on the 12 l=
abels, grouped by study, to stabilize rare-label representation per fold (f=
racture especially).</li>
<li>All preprocessing statistics (normalization percentiles, label co-occur=
rence priors, NLP extraction vocab) computed per training fold only.</li>
<li>Report per-label OOF AUC + macro-AUC + micro-AUC; OOF predictions retai=
ned for ensembling, threshold analysis, and error analysis.</li>
<li><strong>Experiment table</strong> (each row: OOF macro-AUC, worst-label=
 AUC, params, train hours):<ol>
<li>Global 3D CNN, BCE (floor)</li>
<li>2.5D MIL baseline (gated attention, mean-pool series), wBCE</li>
<li><ul>
<li>metadata-conditioned attention + transformer series agg</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><ul>
<li>asym loss + label-embedding head</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Teacher (multimodal)</li>
<li>Student + logit KD</li>
<li><ul>
<li>feature KD</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><ul>
<li>attention KD + ITC</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>3D Swin variant (ensemble diversity)</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>14. Evaluation &amp; calibration</h2>
<p>Metric: mean of 12 per-label ROC-AUCs (threshold-free). Therefore:</p>
<ul>
<li>Accuracy/F1 at 0.5 is misaligned =E2=80=94 optimize <strong>ranking</st=
rong> (AUC-sensitive losses: asymmetric loss explicitly targets hard-exampl=
e ranking).</li>
<li>Calibration matters only for downstream thresholding/debugging, not the=
 leaderboard; still report ECE per label for medical credibility, and calib=
rate with Platt scaling on OOF if any thresholded deliverable is needed.</l=
i>
<li>Watch macro vs micro: a single common-label (effusion) improvement can =
mask a rare-label (fracture) collapse =E2=80=94 always inspect the per-labe=
l table and the <strong>worst-label AUC</strong> as the tie-breaking model-=
selection signal.</li>
<li>Ensembles: probability averaging (after per-label rank/Platt harmonizat=
ion) vs logit averaging =E2=80=94 average <strong>per-label rank-normalized=
 scores</strong> or sigmoid probabilities; rank averaging is robust to per-=
label calibration drift across fold models.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>15. Ensembling</h2>
<ul>
<li>5 folds =C3=97 2=E2=80=933 seeds (different slice sampling seeds), plus=
 architecture diversity: 2.5D-B0 + 2.5D-ConvNeXt-T + one 3D variant if it p=
roved competitive. Teacher and student can both be ensembled (teacher often=
 still uses text; but only student is deployable =E2=80=94 ensemble student=
s).</li>
<li>Probability averaging across all models per label; prefer logit averagi=
ng within same-architecture families (calibration-consistent) and probabili=
ty/rank averaging across families.</li>
</ul>
